<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.14.1: Distinguish Linear and Exponential Growth </item>
  <item> 5.14.2: Using Tables to Compare Linear and Exponential Growth Functions
    <list>
      <item> 5.14.2: Self Check </item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>5.14.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item> 5.14.3: Compare Linear Functions with Exponential Functions 
    <list>
      <item> 5.14.3: Self Check </item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>5.14.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item> 5.14.4: Using Function Notation to Compare Linear and Exponential Functions </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in 5.14.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<para>Graphing technology</para>
<title> Required Preparation</title>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their
  own device. </para>
<para>Be prepared to display a graph for all to see using the embedded Desmos applet or other graphing technology.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look
    for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral
    explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link> </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
